1. Decides to renew until 28 February 2026 the measures imposed by resolution 1844 (2008), as renewed and modified by subsequent resolutions, including the provisions set out in paragraphs 15 and 17 of resolution 2182 (2014), as expanded by paragraph 5 of resolution 2607 (2021) to cover improvised explosive device components, as most recently renewed by paragraph 1 of resolution 2775 (2025); recalls that these measures include the targeted arms embargo, travel ban, asset freeze and charcoal ban; and reaffirms that the arms embargo does not apply to weapons and military equipment destined for the Federal Government of Somalia and its security forces, consistent with resolution 2713 (2023), and applies only to Al-Shabaab, Islamic State in Somalia and other individuals and entities designated by the Committee;

